# RUN: TD=%t.dir && mkdir -p $TD
# RUN: %trust -q --temp-dir $TD -o $TD/rational_example %srcroot/examples/rational.src
# RUN: cd $TD && ./rational_example && echo "PASS"
# CHECK: PASS
# CHECK: 4023872600770937735437024339230

# End-to-end run of the real example `examples/rational.src` (1000! as a Rational):
#   * rational literal `num\den` (a dedicated lexeme RationalLiteral) is constructed
#     directly from the string via `trust::Rational("num\den")`;
#   * `mult := 1` (inferred Bool) is widened to Int64 by `mult += 1`;
#   * `:StrChar(fact)` casts the Rational to std::string via `operator std::string()`;
#   * the entry `@main():={...}` is emitted as `int rational__main__()` (raw name),
#     so it links with the pipeline-generated `_main.cppt` entry point.
# The `@assert(fact == 402387…\1)` is ENABLED BY DEFAULT and actually verifies the result
# (process would abort on mismatch); the program prints the 2568-digit 1000! value.
